    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The first state to bear the name Turk, a steppe khaganate that at its peak stretched from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> towards the Black Sea.</li><li>It protected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> trade, drew vast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> tribute from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and left the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkhon-inscriptions">Orkhon Inscriptions</a>, the oldest major Turkic texts.</li><li>Rival claimants under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lateral-succession">lateral succession</a> and Chinese divide-and-rule broke it twice; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghurs</a> ended it for good in 744.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkhon-inscriptions">Orkhon Inscriptions</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilterish-qaghan">Ilterish Qaghan</a> began rebuilding the fallen Turkic empire in 682 with just seventeen men in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yin-shan">Yin Shan</a> mountains.</p></aside>
    </section>

